    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.cycle_basis - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.cycle_basis.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.cycle_basis()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a fundamental cycle basis of the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.cycle_basis()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a fundamental cycle basis of the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.cycle_basis()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find a fundamental cycle basis of the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind a fundamental cycle basis of the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L37709-L37803){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.cycle_basis(root=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Cycle basis](../assets/graphs/cycle-basis.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The house-shaped graph has 6 edges and 5 nodes, so a cycle basis has 6 − 5 + 1 = 2 cycles. Building the BFS tree from root A (node id 1) gives the fundamental cycles B, A, C (accent color) and D, B, A, C, E (teal), each closed by one non-tree edge.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA cycle basis is a minimal set of cycles such that any cycle in the graph can be expressed\nas a symmetric difference (XOR) of cycles in the basis. For a connected graph with `V`\nvertices and `E` edges, the cycle basis has exactly `E - V + 1` cycles (the cyclomatic\ncomplexity).\n\nThe algorithm builds a spanning tree using BFS from a root node, then for each non-tree edge\n(back edge), finds the fundamental cycle it creates with the tree.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[root]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional root node ID to start BFS from. If `None`, uses an arbitrary node. Different\n    root nodes may produce different (but equally valid) cycle bases.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A list of cycles forming the cycle basis. Each cycle is a list of node IDs. The cycles\n    are fundamental cycles (each contains exactly one back edge).\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If called on a directed graph (cycle basis only applies to undirected graphs).\n\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the specified root node does not exist in the graph.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe cyclomatic number $E - V + C$ (with $C$ the number of connected components)\nfixes the size of *every* fundamental cycle basis, so what varies between choices is\nonly which cycles appear, not how many. Building one takes $O(V + E)$: a BFS\nspanning tree covers the tree edges, and each of the remaining $E - V + C$ back\nedges closes a unique fundamental cycle. Different `root=` choices, or different\nspanning trees more generally, produce different but equally valid bases.\nDisconnected graphs are handled component by component. If total edge weight\nmatters, `minimum_cycle_basis()` finds the basis of least weight.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~minimum_cycle_basis`) \n\n:   A cycle basis of the shortest cycles.\n\n[](`~directed_cycle_basis`) \n\n:   A cycle basis that follows the edges' directions.\n\n[](`~simple_cycles`) \n\n:   Every cycle in the graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA square with a diagonal has three cycles, but any two of them make the third, so the\nbasis has two:\n\n::: {#0781e848 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"A\"), (\"A\", \"C\")]\n)\n\n[[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in c] for c in graph.cycle_basis()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['B', 'C', 'A'], ['D', 'C', 'A']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The rings of caffeine\n\n`molecules()` holds seven small molecules as graphs of their atoms and bonds, with the\nhydrogen atoms left out. Caffeine has 14 atoms and 15 bonds, so a cycle basis has two\ncycles. They need not be its two rings: here the basis has the 6-atom ring and, in the\naccent color, the 9-atom loop around the outside of both rings:\n\n::: {#93f2bee7 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncaffeine = ec.molecules()[\"caffeine\"]\nlabel = caffeine.get_label_from_id\nbasis = caffeine.cycle_basis()\n\n[[label(n) for n in cycle] for cycle in basis]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[['C3', 'N4', 'C6', 'N3', 'C5', 'C4'],\n ['N1', 'C4', 'C5', 'N3', 'C6', 'N4', 'C3', 'N2', 'C2']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#59751a32 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncaffeine.plot(\n    highlight={\n        \"accent\": basis[1] + basis[1][:1],\n        \"soft\": basis[0] + basis[0][:1],\n    },\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=1,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\